    "Model exhibits a persistent upward bias when recent history shows volatility followed by a drop (e.g., Example 1), consistently overestimating the next 30 days.",
    "When sentiment shifts from positive to negative (e.g., Example 3, 4, 5), the model fails to capture immediate mean reversion and instead predicts continued growth or excessive stability.",
    "The model underestimates volatility spikes; it smooths out sharp price increases (like the jump to 76.20 in Examples 1-5) by predicting a slower, linear trajectory.",
    "In high-volatility regimes with mixed sentiment, the model's forecast horizon is too long-term and lacks responsiveness to short-term sentiment reversals.",
    "Apply a downward correction factor of approximately 3-5% to the model's initial forecast when recent history ends with a price decline or neutral sentiment spike."
